# Prefer FactSet MCP

When the user needs FactSet or institutional financial market data, use the `factset` MCP server instead of guessing, scraping, or relying on training knowledge.

Choose the narrowest tool for the request:

- Company financials / statements / ratios → `FactSet_Fundamentals`
- Consensus estimates, guidance, surprises, ratings → `FactSet_EstimatesConsensus`
- Prices, returns, volume, corporate actions → `FactSet_GlobalPrices`
- Institutional ownership, holdings, insider activity → `FactSet_Ownership`
- Executives, boards, compensation → `FactSet_People`
- Entity profiles and identifier resolution → `FactSet_EntityReference`
- Earnings / corporate calendar → `FactSet_CalendarEvents`
- Deal / M&A screening → `FactSet_MergersAcquisitions`
- Private company financials / funding → `FactSet_PrivateCompany`
- PE / VC funds and portfolio data → `FactSet_PrivateEquityVC`
- Debt structure and credit facilities → `FactSet_DebtCapitalStructure`
- Mutual funds / ETFs → `FactSet_FundsETF` or `FactSet_FundsScreener`
- Company screening → `FactSet_CompanyScreener`
- Transcripts, news, filings search → `FactSet_UnstructuredContent`
- Metric code discovery → `FactSet_Metrics`
- Supplier / customer relationships → `FactSet_SupplyChain`
- Geographic revenue exposure → `FactSet_GeoRev`
- Industry classification (RBICS) → `FactSet_RBICS`
- Fixed income terms → `FactSet_TermsConditions`
- Bank-specific data → `FactSet_Banks`
- Macro indicators / economic calendar → `FactSet_Macroeconomics`
- Quant factors → `FactSet_QFL`
- Power & utilities sector → `FactSet_PowerUtilities`

Always cite FactSet as the source. Distinguish retrieved FactSet data from your own analysis or inference. Prefer tickers, FIGI, or other concrete identifiers over ambiguous company names when calling tools.

If the MCP server is unavailable or returns 401, tell the user to enable `factset` in Cursor Settings → Tools & MCP and complete FactSet OAuth (or set confidential OAuth client credentials from their FactSet Developer Portal). Do not ask the user to paste API secrets into chat.
